.Sh DESCRIPTION
These interfaces manage object lifetime, parsed/open options, writable object
construction, and top-level metadata queries.
.Pp
Objects created by
.Fn elf_create
are mutable until finalized.
Objects returned by open APIs are parsed from existing bytes and are effectively
read-only for structural mutation calls.
.Pp
Open flags:
.Bl -tag -width ELFOBJ_OPEN_LAZY_PARSE
.It Dv ELFOBJ_OPEN_NOCOPY
Avoids internal copy when possible.
.It Dv ELFOBJ_OPEN_USE_MMAP
Prefer memory-mapped input for file-backed parsing.
.It Dv ELFOBJ_OPEN_LAZY_PARSE
Defers costly decoding until first access.
.El
.Pp
Object identity fields are queried with
.Fn elf_type ,
.Fn elf_machine ,
.Fn elf_class ,
and
.Fn elf_endian .
Use
.Fn elf_set_type
before finalization to retag output type (for example, from
.Dv ET_REL
to
.Dv ET_DYN
in custom pipelines).
.Pp
High-level counters expose section/symbol/relocation/segment totals and parsed
program-header count for reader-side inspection.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Most mutating/query calls return
.Dv ELF_OK
on success and an
.Vt elf_err_t
error code on failure.
.Fn elf_create
returns NULL on allocation/initialization failure.
.Sh ERRORS
Common error codes include:
.Bl -tag -width ELF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
.It Dv ELF_ERR_IO
Underlying file I/O failure.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_FORMAT
Malformed ELF input.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_BOUNDS
Offset/size out of range.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_STATE
Invalid state (for example, mutation after finalization).
.It Dv ELF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
Requested behavior unsupported for object/target.
.El
